   "reading": "the New Testament corpus is a set of texts with a date of collection: 'The Christian New Testament is not a book. It is Athanasius of Alexandria, 367 CE, Festal Letter 39.' (#674); the rival collections stand beside it (#978); the label and the definite article survive the facts ('*the* Bible, *the* New Testament'); the corrected thesis reads the canonical texts as the workshop tradition's most successful products; at John 1:1 and 1:14 the Word's flesh is read as text: 'The body the Word prepared for itself is the codex.' (#978), bounded: 'Both readings are textually defensible'",
   "state": "#978 the current state (FRACTURE.02, a recomposition of v1.0–v3.0 and the Manifesto); #674 the prior state, the Manifesto's compression, revised by #978 where #978 says so (18 revises edges in 04-arguments.jsonl)",
   "seating_note": "#65 is titled 'Counterfeit Orthodoxies — A Dialectical Fracture Through the Citation Map', and its seated text is FRACTURE.02, the recomposition #978 carries, sentence for sentence (two lines differ, checked 2026-11-09). Carried as data; the v1.0–v3.0 text the title names is not seated in this repository; its recovery is the author's to rule",
   "statement": "stmt:20261109-1556"
  },
